  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A first name and the family name, traditionally the father's; since 2014 parents may give the mother's name or both. Flemish family names often start with Van, Vanden, De or Ver (Van Damme, De Smet, Verhaegen) and are written with or without a space depending on the family. Walloon and Brussels names are mostly French. Belgians of Moroccan, Turkish, Congolese and Italian heritage are a big part of Brussels, Antwerp, Liège and Charleroi, and the EU institutions bring people from every member state.",
